MEASUREMENT -- what the dress-after ordering omits
  lattice 2 x 4 x 4, pitch 0.25 km, planes (18, 19)
  identical illumination and T-matrices; ONLY G0 differs
==============================================================================

   reflector       Q     T  |dG0|/|G0|  |psi_A-psi_B|/|psi_A|    Born est
         0.0       2   0.3   1.276e-09              9.216e-11   9.259e-11
         0.0       2   1.0   1.276e-09              2.965e-10   3.013e-10
         0.0   10000   0.3   9.029e-01              2.583e-02   2.471e-02
         0.0   10000   1.0   9.029e-01              1.288e-01   7.689e-02
         0.3   10000   0.3   9.067e-01              7.364e-02   7.216e-02
         0.3   10000   1.0   9.067e-01              2.545e-01   2.145e-01
         1.0   10000   0.3   1.070e+00              2.524e-02   2.587e-02
         1.0   10000   1.0   1.070e+00              8.787e-02   7.819e-02

  Reading it. |dG0|/|G0| is the omitted operator's own size, measured
  without any solve -- the column the whole table hangs on. The Q = 2
  row is the null: heavy attenuation kills the path to the seabed, so
  the omitted coupling is small and the two orderings must nearly
  coincide. That is the control, and it is a control over dG0 rather
  than over the deep reflector, which does NOT remove the seabed.

  The Born column is one application of the omitted term. Where it
  tracks the measured difference, the omission is first-order and
  estimable; where the difference exceeds it, the omitted coupling is
  being compounded by the multiple scattering, which is precisely the
  regime the thesis ordering exists for.
